# Cursor AI Rules for Stickman Animation Website

## Project Context
This is a Stickman Animation Website project that will be deployed on Vercel. The project focuses on creating engaging animations and interactive content.

## Code Style & Standards
- Use modern ES6+ JavaScript/TypeScript syntax
- Follow responsive design principles with mobile-first approach
- Implement accessibility best practices (ARIA labels, semantic HTML)
- Use CSS Grid and Flexbox for layouts
- Prefer functional components over class components
- Use meaningful variable and function names

## Animation & Performance
- Optimize animations for 60fps performance
- Use CSS transforms and opacity for smooth animations
- Implement lazy loading for heavy assets
- Use requestAnimationFrame for JavaScript animations
- Minimize DOM manipulation during animations

## File Organization
- Keep components in a `components/` directory
- Organize styles in a `styles/` directory
- Store utilities in a `utils/` directory
- Use descriptive file names that reflect their purpose
- Group related files in feature-based folders

## Vercel Deployment
- Never run build commands locally (use `git push` for Vercel builds)
- Ensure all environment variables are set in Vercel dashboard
- Use `.vercelignore` to exclude unnecessary files
- Keep build scripts in package.json for Vercel CI/CD

## AI Assistance Preferences
- Provide complete, working code examples
- Include error handling and edge cases
- Suggest performance optimizations
- Recommend modern web development best practices
- Help with responsive design implementation

## Testing & Quality
- Suggest unit tests for critical functions
- Recommend accessibility testing tools
- Include error boundary implementations
- Suggest performance monitoring approaches

## Documentation
- Write clear, concise comments for complex logic
- Document component props and usage
- Include setup instructions for new features
- Maintain README with project overview and setup steps
